All `_t` and `_enum` suffixes are gone for types defined in this module; `cnx_t`/`path_t` remain because they're owned by `internal.rs` and renaming them is out of scope for this pass. `cargo check` and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` both pass cleanly from a fresh build.

## Summary

I idiomized the Phase 1 stub of `rs/fq/src/cc_common.rs` along three axes. **Naming**: `min_max_rtt_t` → `MinMaxRtt`, `newreno_alg_state_t` → `NewRenoAlgState` (variants `SlowStart` / `CongestionAvoidance`), `newreno_sim_state_t` → `NewRenoSimState`; the `#[allow(non_camel_case_types)]` lint suppressions are gone, and `Default` is now derived where the C semantics imply zero-init. **API shape**: the nine `cc_*` free functions whose primary argument was a `cnx_t` or `path_t` collapse into inherent methods on those types (`impl cnx_t { fn cc_sequence_number(&self, …) }`, `impl path_t { fn cc_lowest_not_ack(&self) }`, etc.), so callers will write `cnx.cc_ack_number(path)` instead of `cc_get_ack_number(&cnx, &path)`. **Borrow shape**: every helper that the C source proves to be read-only — including `NewRenoSimState::notify`'s `cnx`/`path_x` arguments — now takes `&` instead of `&mut`, replacing the previous "be conservative until Phase 3" stance with the correct shape derivable from the C bodies. Doc comments were rewritten to lead with what the Rust API does and cite the `picoquic_*` C symbol for traceability rather than leaning on `C: …` as the only description. No callers in sibling modules referenced the renamed types, so the change is self-contained.


